      ],
      "impact": "The LiDAR header loads the main I2C bus and, if a module is plugged in, its control pin is tied to the EZO isolator power-disable net, which could hold PDIS and disable the pH/EC channels — wiring not intended for this revision.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the specified design: most convincingly, the VREF divider bottom resistors R27/R29 on the Nutrient-A/B TMC2209 drivers are 10.7 MΩ instead of the 10.7 kΩ used on the pH-Down driver (R25), driving those dosing pumps at maximum current; additionally the ATO-valve switch is an AO3400A rather than the specified AON6407, and the supposedly unwired TF-Luna LiDAR header is connected to +5V, the I2C bus and EZO_PDIS."
}

